==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*syewH-}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*šiti}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*sjū́ˀtei}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*syewH-}}.
Cognate to {{cog|lt|siūti}}, {{cog|en|sew}}, {{cog|la|suō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ши́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-шить.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|ɨtʲ|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|шить|impf|pf=сшить|vn=шитьё,шве́ние<q:dated>}}

# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[sew]]
#: {{syn|ru|прошива́ть|стега́ть|смётывать|строчи́ть|тача́ть}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''шить''' [[на]] [[машинка|маши́нке]]|to sew on a machine}}
# {{lb|ru|intransitive|only|_|imperfective}} to be occupied with sewing, to [[tailor]]
#: {{syn|ru|обшива́ть|портняжить}}
#: {{uxi|ru|Чем [[она́]] [[заниматься|занима́ется]]? Она '''шьёт'''.|What is she? She’s a dressmaker.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[order]] (e.g., a dress)
# {{lb|ru|only|_|imperfective}} to [[embroider]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''шить''' [[золото|зо́лотом]]|embroider [[in]] [[gold]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|шито [[белый|бе́лыми]] [[нитка|ни́тками]]|q=saying|blatantly obvious, transparent to anyone|lit=embroidered in white thread}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''шить''' [[де́ло]]|q=colloquial|to cook up [[charges]]|lit=to embroider the case}}
#: {{uxi|ru|([[он]]) [[не]] [[лыко|лы́ком]] шит|q=saying|(he) was not born yesterday|lit=(he) was not embroidered in [[bast]]}}
# {{lb|ru|figuratively}} to [[nail]] [[planking]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''шить''' [[плот]]|to make a [[raft]]}}

